            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3832-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-3832 medium vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gnutls. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by presenting a specially crafted Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) response during a TLS handshake. Due to a logic error in how gnutls processes multi-record OCSP responses, a client with OCSP verification enabled may incorrectly accept a revoked server certificate, potentially leading to a compromise of trust."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-3832",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-3832\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libgnutls30\nVersion: 3.7.3-4ubuntu1.8\nFix Version: 3.7.3-4ubuntu1.9\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-3832](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-3832)",
